hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19289","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threading through the people on the Day of Hunayn asking about the dwelling of Khalid ibn al-Walid. A drunk was brought, and he ordered those with him to beat him with what was in their hands."
"19290","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us from al-Zuhri that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the conquest expedition, and I was a young lad, threading through the people asking about the dwelling of Khalid ibn al-Walid. A drinker was brought, and he ordered him beaten with what was in their hands. Some beat him with his sandal, some beat him with a stick, some beat him with a whip. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw dust upon him."
"19291","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar used to narrate from Khalid ibn al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah: He went out that day commanding the cavalry of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibn Azhar said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after Allah routed the disbelievers and the Muslims returned to their dwellings, walking among the Muslims saying: Who guides to the lodging of Khalid ibn al-Walid? I walked or hastened before him, and I was adolescent, saying: Who guides to the lodging of Khalid ibn al-Walid, until we threaded to his lodging. Khalid was leaning on the back of his saddle. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and looked at his wound. Al-Zuhri said: I think he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) blew upon it."
"19292","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Salih, and Ibn Shihab narrated that Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar used to narrate that he attended the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was throwing dust in their faces. My father said: This follows the hadith of al-Zuhri from Qabisah about the drinker of wine."
